# Data and AI

Follow `docs/architecture/data-policy.md`. The planner recommends only approved destinations, places, hotels, and activities already in the catalog. It uses no open-web search, browsing, or external destination discovery. Model output and provider payloads create no approved catalog entities.

An approved provider API may refresh permitted dynamic fields on an existing approved record. Each write keeps provenance, checked and verified timestamps, a validation result, and an append-only log. A failed or skipped refresh is not verification.

Invent no price, availability, booking confirmation, or visa requirement. Unknown data stays unknown.

Keep estimates, quotes, booking requests, and confirmed bookings as separate states.

```ts
// Bad — invented hotel and a request treated as booked
{ name: "Grand Palace", price: 180, status: "confirmed" }

// Good — approved id, price unknown until revalidation succeeds
{ hotelId: approvedHotel.id, price: null, status: "booking_request" }
```
